# pyenv
#   For a library or app, you might want to share your .python-version if you're
#   using tools like pyenv. But for local use, it can be ignored:
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in git.
#   However, in case you're running an extension, feel free to ignore or not:
# Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similarly, In case you're using poetry, you'll want to include poetry.lock but exclude:
# .poetry

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, pdm.lock is usually tracked in git. But some files should be ignored:
# .pdm-plugins/
# .pdm-build/

# PEP 582; project packages folder (e.g. pdm)
__pypackages__/

